
Absolutely. For a **Java Full Stack Developer with ~5 years experience**, I would not limit preparation to the 15 scenarios you already have.

A strong interview can move from:

**Core Java → Spring → Spring Boot → REST → JPA/DB → Microservices → Kafka → Security → Testing → React → AWS/Docker/K8s → CI/CD → Observability → System Design → Production scenarios.**

Recent full-stack interview reports also show this broader mix: Core Java/JVM, Spring Boot/Security, REST, microservices, SQL/JPA, React, cloud/deployment, system design and production scenarios. ([LinkedIn][1])

## 🎯 I would build your master bank as ~200 scenario questions

Not 200 random questions. **Grouped by topic**, so you can make a proper mind map.

